From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Subject: [PATCH] serial: lantiq: keep UART alive in shutdown when port is console

When the lantiq UART port is also serving as the kernel console,
lqasc_shutdown() must not disable the controller or gate its clock.
The TTY layer invokes uart_ops::shutdown when the last userspace FD
referencing the port goes away (typically late during system shutdown,
when init kills the getty / login shells holding /dev/console open).
After this point the kernel still needs to be able to emit printk
output via lqasc_console_write() - for the remainder of orderly
reboot, and especially for panic and sysrq paths - which writes
directly to LTQ_ASC_TBUF and polls LTQ_ASC_FSTAT for FIFO drain.
Both depend on CON being enabled and the clock running.

The current code unconditionally writes 0 to LTQ_ASC_CON and calls
clk_disable_unprepare() on the UART clock. On platforms where init
closes the last reference before reboot completes (e.g. procd's
STATE_HALT path on OpenWrt), this kills the controller mid-shutdown:
any subsequent userspace write to /dev/console blocks forever in
uart_write() waiting for a FIFO that can no longer drain, and printk
output via the console driver disappears too. The system stops
making progress and never reaches reboot(2), even though the kernel
is otherwise fine.

Skip the controller-disable and clk_disable_unprepare() calls when
uart_console(port) is true. The FIFO flushes (and free_irq) are kept
unconditionally, matching the pattern used by other Linux serial
drivers that share their UART with the kernel console (imx, atmel,
xilinx_uartps, ...).

Encountered while bringing up the MaxLinear URX/Lightning Mountain
SoC, which uses drivers/tty/serial/lantiq.c with a single ASC port
serving both ttyLTQ0 and the kernel console.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/lantiq.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/lantiq.c
@@ -370,17 +370,27 @@ lqasc_shutdown(struct uart_port *port)
 {
 	struct ltq_uart_port *ltq_port = to_ltq_uart_port(port);
 	unsigned long flags;
+	bool is_console = uart_console(port);
 
 	ltq_port->soc->free_irq(port);
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&ltq_port->lock, flags);
-	__raw_writel(0, port->membase + LTQ_ASC_CON);
+	/*
+	 * If this port is also serving as the kernel console, do not turn
+	 * the controller off or gate its clock. lqasc_console_write() needs
+	 * the hardware live (CON enabled, clock running) to flush printk
+	 * output during system shutdown / panic / sysrq, after the last TTY
+	 * user has closed and userspace stops referencing /dev/console.
+	 * Only flush the FIFOs.
+	 */
+	if (!is_console)
+		__raw_writel(0, port->membase + LTQ_ASC_CON);
 	asc_update_bits(ASCRXFCON_RXFEN, ASCRXFCON_RXFFLU,
 		port->membase + LTQ_ASC_RXFCON);
 	asc_update_bits(ASCTXFCON_TXFEN, ASCTXFCON_TXFFLU,
 		port->membase + LTQ_ASC_TXFCON);
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&ltq_port->lock, flags);
-	if (!IS_ERR(ltq_port->clk))
+	if (!is_console && !IS_ERR(ltq_port->clk))
 		clk_disable_unprepare(ltq_port->clk);
 }
 
